# SYSTEM 10: ADAPTIVE TUTOR ORCHESTRATOR

## System Name

Adaptive Tutor Orchestrator

## Product Purpose

This system upgrades Ada from a generic chat assistant into a mode-aware, context-aware, skill-aware tutor.

## Why This System Exists

A normal chatbot gives answers. Ada must teach, guide, debug, challenge, and protect learning value.

## Tech Stack

Recommended implementation:

* Ada tutor backend route
* LLM provider abstraction
* prompt assembly service
* project/step context loader
* skill graph context loader
* validation result context loader
* tutor event logging
* mode policy engine
* leakage guard
* token budget control

## Ada Context Inputs

Ada should use:

* current step context
* selected mode
* learner skill graph
* last error
* validation result
* hint usage
* project goal
* role goal

## Adaptive Behavior Examples

> Beginner + repeated failure → explain concept simply
> Intermediate + one failure → ask diagnostic question
> Independent mode → minimal hint, no solution
> Capstone mode → behave like interviewer/reviewer

## Tutor Mode Rules

Guided Mode:

* explain more
* provide scaffolding
* allow stronger hints

Hint-Based Mode:

* provide progressive hints
* avoid full solution too early

Independent Mode:

* ask diagnostic questions
* avoid solution leakage
* keep feedback minimal

Adaptive Mode:

* select help level based on learner evidence
* adjust over time

## Acceptance Criteria

This system is complete when:

* Ada receives project/step/mode context
* Ada respects mode policy
* Ada logs tutor events
* Ada avoids answer leakage in Independent Mode
* Ada uses validation failure context
* Ada can recommend next actions based on skill gaps

